The household's sky changes often but is never hostile — favorable windows for different efforts open in different months. Work in seasons: one push for bonding and visits, one for formal matters, one for rest and the home itself, spread across the year. Avoid staking the whole household on one long bet; three small moves track this sky better. Beneath the seasons, existing routines and elders stay as the steady base. Accept help offers from relatives immediately and on standard terms. Keep eyes on the calendar and a one-month buffer of calm. Consistent presence is what family members remember in changeable weather — and it quietly turns into trust by December.

